  "notes": "Borrower NSGL only had one non-original workbook to process: NSGL_Loan_Restructured.xlsx (the file NSGL_Loan.xlsx is the ORIGINAL, already represented by EX_DATA['NSGL'] in examples.ts, and was used only as a diff baseline, not as a separate event).\n\nMethodology: I diffed every sheet of NSGL_Loan_Restructured.xlsx cell-by-cell against the original NSGL_Loan.xlsx. The two files are structurally identical (same sheets: Disbursement, Summary, NSGL_Loan, Accrual_NSGL, Repayment Schedule) and share identical header parameters (loan amount 980,000,000 BDT, 9% rate, 360-day basis, Level Principal, monthly frequency, same two disbursements on 2020-02-16 and 2020-03-25, nominal 96-month/90-installment original schedule). The divergence begins at the row for 2020-09-15 (installment 1 of the original 6-month-moratorium schedule):\n- In NSGL_Loan.xlsx, interest for Mar-Aug 2020 is paid in cash each month (closing balance flat at 980,000,000) and principal amortization of 10,888,888.89/month begins 2020-09-15, finishing exactly at installment 90 (2028-02-15) with closing balance 0.\n- In NSGL_Loan_Restructured.xlsx, interest for the same Mar-Dec 2020 window is instead CAPITALIZED into principal each month (opening balance climbs 700,000,000 -> 1,048,726,482.20 by 2021-01-14), the principal moratorium is extended by 4 more months (first principal payment moves from 2020-09-15 to 2021-01-14), and a cell explicitly labeled \"Tenure Extension - 1st Restructuring\" appears at the point the schedule extends past the original 90th installment (period 87 of 95 in the new schedule, dated 2028-03-15, is annotated as the tenure-extension marker, with the schedule now running 95 installments total through 2028-11-15 instead of 90 through 2028-02-15).\n\nI modeled this single event as effective 2021-01-14 (the first repayment date under the new/capitalized regime), with the new \"loan_amount\"-equivalent (opening balance at that date) of 1,048,726,482.1966648 rolled forward as a single disbursement, capitalizedAmount = 1,048,726,482.1966648 - 980,000,000 = 68,726,482.20 (the interest capitalized into principal during the extended 10-month moratorium vs. the original 6-month moratorium with cash interest payments), waivedAmount = 0 (no forgiveness detected — only capitalization), overdueAmountRolledIn = 0 (no arrears/overdue rolled in; this was a proactive/scheduled capitalization+extension, not a default-driven reschedule of overdue amounts), rate unchanged at 9% (no rate change — hence eventType RESTRUCTURE rather than RATE_CHANGE, since both moratorium/tenor and capitalization changed), tenor extended from 96 to ~105 months (90->95 installments, all still monthly).\n\nBecause the workbook's post-event installment amounts (level principal of 11,039,226.128385946/month plus declining-balance interest) could not be cleanly re-derived as \"the same 11,039,226.13 principal each period is a clean function of loan_amount/remaining installments\" without floating-point drift matching the workbook exactly, I used the override arrays (opening_balance_amounts, interest_payment_amounts, closing_balance_amounts) pinned row-by-row to the workbook's actual figures — mirroring the approach used for MCML/QPSL/SCBL/SKS/THERMAX in examples.ts. The schedule fully amortizes to a closing balance of ~0 (1.445e-6, floating point residue) at the final installment (2028-11-15), confirming this restructured version is the final/terminal version for NSGL — no further reschedule/restructure workbook exists for this borrower.\n\nNo explicit regulatory reference (e.g., \"DFIM Circular\", \"BB approval\") was found anywhere in the workbook text, so regulatoryReference is null. No separate co-financier tranche or additional facility was found — NSGL has a single IDCOL facility."
